*=======================================================================
* pyrazine -- Kallen-Lehmann ingredients for the OpenMolcas 2027 contribution
*
* Produces, for a single molecule and in one job:
*   - Dyson orbitals d^n  (RASSI DYSOn)   -> the spectral WEIGHTS
*   - MS-CASPT2 state energies            -> the exact POLES  IP_n
* which is everything  G_rs(E_F) = SUM_n d_r^n d_s^n / (E_F - IP_n)
* needs.  Kallen reads them out of the standard Molden export.
*
* Geometry: B3LYP/cc-pVDZ minimum (see pyrazine_opt.input), planar, C2v in
* fact but run in C1 on purpose -- the NAO construction needs a fixed
* desymmetrised AO ordering, and atom indices must not be renumbered
* between the optimisation and this job.
*
* Active space: the ten frontier orbitals -- five highest occupied and
* five lowest virtual by RHF energy -- i.e. CAS(10,10) for the neutral
* and CAS(9,10) for the cation, on the same orbitals.
* The five highest occupied span both nitrogen lone pairs n+(6ag) and n-(5b1u) and the upper pi manifold -- the n/pi ordering is the point.
*
* JOB001 MUST be the neutral: RASSI's Dyson loop runs JSTATE=1..DYSEXPSF
* over initial states and ISTATE=JSTATE+1..NSTATE over final states
* (src/rassi/writedys.f), so the N-electron state has to come first.
*=======================================================================

&GATEWAY
  coord = pyrazine_opt.Opt.xyz
  basis = cc-pVDZ
  group = c1

&SEWARD

* Closed-shell RHF: fixes the energy ordering the active space is cut from.
&SCF

*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* N-electron reference: neutral singlet, CAS(10,10)
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
&RASSCF
  Title    = pyrazine neutral CAS(10,10)
  Spin     = 1
  Charge   = 0
  nActEl   = 10 0 0
  Inactive = 16
  Ras2     = 10
  CIRoot   = 1 1 1

* Natural orbitals of the N-electron reference define the NAO basis.
* Their occupations are FRACTIONAL -- the density must be occupation-
* weighted, not cut at occ >= 1.
>>COPY $Project.rasscf.molden  pyrazine_neutral.rasscf.molden
>>COPY $Project.JobIph         JOB001

&CASPT2
  Title      = CASPT2 on the neutral reference
  Multistate = 1 1
  Imaginary  = 0.1

*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* XMULtistate, not MULtistate.  The cation manifold here is strongly
* mixed -- in thiophene that mixing IS the pole-strength collapse the
* example exists to measure, and in pyrazine it is the contested
* ordering of the lone-pair and pi states.  Ordinary MS-CASPT2 is not
* invariant to rotations within a state-averaged space, so inside a
* near-degenerate manifold its answer depends on the CASSCF root basis
* it happened to be handed.  XMS diagonalises H0 within that space
* first and removes the dependence.  Both molecules use it, for
* comparability.  (MS-CASPT2 also runs to completion here -- XMS is
* chosen on the physics, not to work around a failure.)
* Poles are therefore read with --poles mscaspt2 (the reader's
* 'X?MS-CASPT2 Root' pattern); the neutral contributes its MS row.
* (N-1)-electron final states: cation doublets, 8 roots -> 8 poles
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
&RASSCF
  Title    = pyrazine cation CAS(9,10), 8 roots
  Spin     = 2
  Charge   = 1
  nActEl   = 9 0 0
  Inactive = 16
  Ras2     = 10
  CIRoot   = 8 8 1

>>COPY $Project.JobIph  JOB002

&CASPT2
  Title      = XMS-CASPT2 on the cation doublets
  XMultistate = 8 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8
  Imaginary  = 0.1

*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Dyson orbitals and amplitudes.
*
* The Molden coefficients are the UN-NORMALISED Dyson orbitals; their
* squared norm IS the pole strength (src/rassi/mkdysorb.f:117).  Do not
* normalise on read -- that silently deletes the spectral weights.
*
* Do NOT take the poles from the Molden Ene= field: molden_dysorb.f:814
* writes F10.4, truncating at 1e-4 Ha.  Difference the MS-CASPT2 state
* energies in this output instead, at full precision.
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
&RASSI
  NrOfJobIphs = 2  1 8
  1
  1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8
  DYSOn
  DYSExport
  1 0
